gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":["paper"],"description_full":"Cirrus Logic, Inc., a fabless semiconductor company, develops mixed-signal processing solutions and audio products in China, the United States, and internationally. The company offers audio products, including amplifiers; codecs components that integrate analog-to-digital converters (ADCs) and digital-to-analog converters (DACs) into a single integrated circuit (IC); smart codecs, a codec with integrated digital signal processing; standalone digital signal processors; and SoundClear technology for use in smartphones, PCs, tablets, AR/VR headsets, wearables, home theatre systems, automotive entertainment systems, and professional audio systems. It also provides camera controllers, haptic and sensing solutions, and battery and power ICs for smartphones, as well as products for automotive, industrial, and imaging applications. The company markets and sells its products through direct sales force, external sales representatives, and distributors. Cirrus Logic, Inc. was incorporated in 1984 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John M. Forsyth | CEO, President & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $386K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $50K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Cirrus Logic, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $5.5B market cap on $2.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 50% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $637M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 32 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.57\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (43% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 19.3% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 9% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 16% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 25% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 36% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Responsive Playbooks and the CRUS Inflection","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/101/Responsive_Playbooks_and_the_CRUS_Inflection_112026013201_1795199521.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795199521.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Don't Overlook Cirrus Logic (CRUS) International Revenue Trends While Assessing the Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3030157/don-t-overlook-cirrus-logic-crus-international-revenue-trends-while-assessing-the-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm_international_revenues-3030157","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794834903.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Cirrus Logic, Inc. (CRUS) \u2013 What Are Brokerages Thinking About This Stock?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/cirrus-logic-inc-crus-what-are-brokerages-thinking-about-this-stock.html","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794828719.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"4,690 Cirrus Logic, I